                                            <td class="timespent"></td>
                                            <td class="workratio">&nbsp;
</td>
                                            <td class="subtasks">                </td>
                                            <td class="issuelinks">                </td>
                                            <td class="environment"></td>
                                            <td class="description">      Invocation of a JAX-RS method may depend on some application classes which may not be loaded already, they will be loaded during invocation. But during invocation the classloader will be CXF war application classloader, this will lead to NoClassDefFoundErrors. To avoid this root resource class&#39; classloader should be set on the current thread.<br/>
Similar fix should be applied to provider methods such as readFrom, writeTo etc.
  </td>
