                <tr id="issuerow12416654" rel="12416654" data-issuekey="CXF-2104" class="issuerow">
                                            <td class="project">    CXF
</td>
                                            <td class="issuekey">

    <a class="issue-link" data-issue-key="CXF-2104" href="https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/CXF-2104">CXF-2104</a>
</td>
                                            <td class="summary"><p>
                Caller application hangs in case it uses the polling (Response) method with JAX-WS async mapping and an http error occurs during sending. In case of callback style (AsyncHandler), the client application has no way of getting the exception.
    </p>
</td>
                                            <td class="issuetype"> Bug</td>
                                            <td class="status">
                Closed
    </td>
                                            <td class="priority">   Major
</td>
                                            <td class="resolution">    Fixed
</td>
                                            <td class="assignee">            Daniel Kulp
    </td>
                                            <td class="reporter">            Gyorgy Orban
    </td>
                                            <td class="creator">            Gyorgy Orban
    </td>
                                            <td class="created"> 11/Mar/09 16:09 </td>
                                            <td class="lastViewed"> &nbsp; </td>
                                            <td class="updated"> 24/Apr/09 21:17 </td>
                                            <td class="resolutiondate"> 11/Mar/09 22:39 </td>
                                            <td class="versions">                        2.1.4,                     2.2,                     2.1.5            </td>
                                            <td class="fixVersions">                        2.0.11,                     2.1.5            </td>
                                            <td class="components">                        JAX-WS Runtime            </td>
                                            <td class="duedate">    &nbsp;
</td>
                                            <td class="votes">0</td>
                                            <td class="watches">0</td>
                                            <td class="thumbnail"></td>
                                            <td class="timeoriginalestimate"></td>
                                            <td class="timeestimate"></td>
                                            <td class="timespent"></td>
                                            <td class="workratio">&nbsp;
</td>
                                            <td class="subtasks">                </td>
                                            <td class="issuelinks">                </td>
                                            <td class="environment">      sun jdk 1.5.x, 1.6.x
  </td>
                                            <td class="description">      This happens if, for example, an http 404 occurs at sending. If the caller app wants to retrieve the response using Response&lt;ResponseBean&gt;.get(), it hangs forever. If it implements the AsynHandler&lt;ResponseBean&gt; method, handleResponse never gets called, which means that the app does not get notified of the exception. The attached patches are against<br/>
http://fisheye6.atlassian.com/browse/~raw,r=651669/cxf/trunk/rt/core/src/main/java/org/apache/cxf/interceptor/ClientOutFaultObserver.java<br/>
and<br/>
http://fisheye6.atlassian.com/browse/~raw,r=743441/cxf/trunk/rt/frontend/jaxws/src/main/java/org/apache/cxf/jaxws/JaxWsClientProxy.java
  </td>
