    </td>
                                            <td class="created"> 08/May/09 06:48 </td>
                                            <td class="lastViewed"> &nbsp; </td>
                                            <td class="updated"> 03/Aug/09 20:06 </td>
                                            <td class="resolutiondate"> 30/Jun/09 16:14 </td>
                                            <td class="versions">                        2.2.1            </td>
                                            <td class="fixVersions">                        2.0.12,                     2.1.6,                     2.2.3            </td>
                                            <td class="components">                        Configuration            </td>
                                            <td class="duedate">    &nbsp;
</td>
                                            <td class="votes">0</td>
                                            <td class="watches">0</td>
                                            <td class="thumbnail"></td>
                                            <td class="timeoriginalestimate"></td>
                                            <td class="timeestimate"></td>
                                            <td class="timespent"></td>
                                            <td class="workratio">&nbsp;
</td>
                                            <td class="subtasks">                </td>
                                            <td class="issuelinks">                </td>
                                            <td class="environment"></td>
                                            <td class="description">      Can the Jsr250BeanPostProcessor def please be changed to :<br/>
&lt;bean id=&quot;org.apache.cxf.bus.spring.Jsr250BeanPostProcessor&quot; class=&quot;org.apache.cxf.bus.spring.Jsr250BeanPostProcessor&quot;&gt;<br/>
     &lt;property name=&quot;bus&quot; ref=&quot;cxf&quot;/&gt;<br/>
&lt;/bean&gt;<br/>
<br/>
Using @Resource with a PostBeanProcessor causes FactoryBeans to create their bean before all PostProcessorBeans are created.<br/>
E.g. JndiObjectFactoryBean, a lookup is forced because spring wants to find all the beans that match the Bus interface. 
  </td>
