                <tr id="issuerow12424938" rel="12424938" data-issuekey="CXF-2212" class="issuerow">
                                            <td class="project">    CXF
</td>
                                            <td class="issuekey">

    <a class="issue-link" data-issue-key="CXF-2212" href="https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/CXF-2212">CXF-2212</a>
</td>
                                            <td class="summary"><p>
                SAAJInInterceptor creates a SAAJ SOAPFault with only one &quot;Detail&quot; child
    </p>
</td>
                                            <td class="issuetype"> Bug</td>
                                            <td class="status">
                Closed
    </td>
                                            <td class="priority">   Major
</td>
                                            <td class="resolution">    Fixed
</td>
                                            <td class="assignee">            Daniel Kulp
    </td>
                                            <td class="reporter">            Colm O hEigeartaigh
    </td>
                                            <td class="creator">            Colm O hEigeartaigh
    </td>
                                            <td class="created"> 08/May/09 14:51 </td>
                                            <td class="lastViewed"> &nbsp; </td>
                                            <td class="updated"> 04/Jun/09 21:32 </td>
                                            <td class="resolutiondate"> 08/May/09 17:11 </td>
                                            <td class="versions">                        2.1.5,                     2.2.1            </td>
                                            <td class="fixVersions">                        2.2.2,                     2.0.12,                     2.1.6            </td>
                                            <td class="components">                        Soap Binding            </td>
                                            <td class="duedate">    &nbsp;
</td>
                                            <td class="votes">0</td>
                                            <td class="watches">0</td>
                                            <td class="thumbnail"></td>
                                            <td class="timeoriginalestimate"></td>
                                            <td class="timeestimate"></td>
                                            <td class="timespent"></td>
                                            <td class="workratio">&nbsp;
</td>
                                            <td class="subtasks">                </td>
                                            <td class="issuelinks">                </td>
                                            <td class="environment"></td>
                                            <td class="description">      <br/>
The SAAJInInterceptor creates a SAAJ SOAPFault with only one &quot;Detail&quot; child. For example, if a SOAP Fault is received with:<br/>
<br/>
&lt;detail&gt;&lt;errorcode&gt;3&lt;/errorcode&gt;&lt;errorstring&gt;This is a fault detail error string&lt;/errorstring&gt;&lt;/detail&gt;<br/>
<br/>
The following code in SAAJInInterceptor will only add a detail element with a single child element to the SOAPFault object that is created:<br/>
<br/>
soapFault.addDetail().appendChild(<br/>
    soapMessage.getSOAPPart().importNode(<br/>
        fault.getDetail().getFirstChild(), true));<br/>
<br/>
And so the output will be:<br/>
<br/>
&lt;detail&gt;&lt;errorcode&gt;3&lt;/errorcode&gt;&lt;/detail&gt;<br/>
<br/>
This is clearly a bug, as the SOAP specs allow for multiple detail child elements. Even worse, it doesn&#39;t take into account the fact that fault.getDetail() could be of type e.g Node.TEXT, and it could just end up adding a newline character. 
  </td>
