                <tr id="issuerow12424976" rel="12424976" data-issuekey="CXF-2213" class="issuerow">
                                            <td class="project">    CXF
</td>
                                            <td class="issuekey">

    <a class="issue-link" data-issue-key="CXF-2213" href="https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/CXF-2213">CXF-2213</a>
</td>
                                            <td class="summary"><p>
                Currently CXF always produces true/false value for for mustUnderstand attribute irrespective of the SOAP version on the wire
    </p>
</td>
                                            <td class="issuetype"> Bug</td>
                                            <td class="status">
                Closed
    </td>
                                            <td class="priority">   Major
</td>
                                            <td class="resolution">    Fixed
</td>
                                            <td class="assignee">            Daniel Kulp
    </td>
                                            <td class="reporter">            Marat Bedretdinov
    </td>
                                            <td class="creator">            Marat Bedretdinov
    </td>
                                            <td class="created"> 08/May/09 22:28 </td>
                                            <td class="lastViewed"> &nbsp; </td>
                                            <td class="updated"> 04/Jun/09 21:32 </td>
                                            <td class="resolutiondate"> 09/May/09 01:06 </td>
                                            <td class="versions">                        2.1.5            </td>
                                            <td class="fixVersions">                        2.2.2,                     2.0.12,                     2.1.6            </td>
                                            <td class="components">                        Soap Binding            </td>
                                            <td class="duedate">    &nbsp;
</td>
                                            <td class="votes">0</td>
                                            <td class="watches">0</td>
                                            <td class="thumbnail"></td>
                                            <td class="timeoriginalestimate"></td>
                                            <td class="timeestimate"></td>
                                            <td class="timespent"></td>
                                            <td class="workratio">&nbsp;
</td>
                                            <td class="subtasks">                </td>
                                            <td class="issuelinks">                </td>
                                            <td class="environment"></td>
                                            <td class="description">      Currently CXF will always produce true/false value for for mustUnderstand attribute irrespective of the SOAP version <br/>
<br/>
1. For SOAP 1.1 spec for mustUnderstand attribute the values should be 0/1 according to http://schemas.xmlsoap.org/soap/envelope/ and http://www.w3.org/TR/2000/NOTE-SOAP-20000508/#_Toc478383500<br/>
<br/>
2. For SOAP 1.2 spec for mustUnderstand attribute the values should be true/false according to http://www.w3.org/2003/05/soap-envelope/ and http://www.w3.org/TR/2003/REC-soap12-part1-20030624/#soapmu 
  </td>
