  </td>
                                            <td class="description">         I&#39;m new to cxf and trying to get a signed message passed between a<br/>
&gt; client and server. I started from an existing ws-policy which works with<br/>
&gt; axis2/rampart, used the cxf version of wsdl2java to generate all the<br/>
&gt; code. Then merged a few things from<br/>
&gt; apache-cxf-2.2.1/samples/ws_security/interopfest/wssec10.<br/>
&gt; The message appears to be formatted and signed correctly by the client,<br/>
&gt; but the server gets a null pointer exception in<br/>
&gt; org.apache.ws.security.message.token.X509Security.getX509Certificate<br/>
&gt; (X509Security.java:92) when processing the incoming message. I looked at<br/>
&gt; the code and it has found the certificate and is faulting because crypt<br/>
&gt; is null.
