                                            <td class="environment">      Windows XP/ Tomcat 6.0.18
  </td>
                                            <td class="description">      I created web service with one-way operation, using wsdl2java (CXF 2.2).<br/>
CXF does not generate fault message in case of fault  (e.g. when it is invoked with wrong message (according to XSD))<br/>
Instead I&#39;m getting HTTP 500 on client side and exception with following stack trace on Tomcat console:<br/>
<br/>
2009-06-08 09:01:11 org.apache.cxf.phase.PhaseInterceptorChain doIntercept<br/>
INFO: Interceptor has thrown exception, unwinding now<br/>
org.apache.cxf.interceptor.Fault: Unmarshalling Error: cvc-datatype-valid.1.2.1: &#39;2009-32-12&#39; is not a valid value for &#39;dateTime&#39;. <br/>
