                <tr id="issuerow12428946" rel="12428946" data-issuekey="CXF-2318" class="issuerow">
                                            <td class="project">    CXF
</td>
                                            <td class="issuekey">

    <a class="issue-link" data-issue-key="CXF-2318" href="https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/CXF-2318">CXF-2318</a>
</td>
                                            <td class="summary"><p>
                Invalid message created when using MTOM and WS-RM
    </p>
</td>
                                            <td class="issuetype"> Bug</td>
                                            <td class="status">
                Closed
    </td>
                                            <td class="priority">   Major
</td>
                                            <td class="resolution">    Fixed
</td>
                                            <td class="assignee">            Daniel Kulp
    </td>
                                            <td class="reporter">            Guillaume Porcher
    </td>
                                            <td class="creator">            Guillaume Porcher
    </td>
                                            <td class="created"> 26/Jun/09 10:12 </td>
                                            <td class="lastViewed"> &nbsp; </td>
                                            <td class="updated"> 03/Aug/09 20:07 </td>
                                            <td class="resolutiondate"> 30/Jun/09 15:28 </td>
                                            <td class="versions">                        2.2.2            </td>
                                            <td class="fixVersions">                        2.0.12,                     2.1.6,                     2.2.3            </td>
                                            <td class="components">                        WS-* Components            </td>
                                            <td class="duedate">    &nbsp;
</td>
                                            <td class="votes">1</td>
                                            <td class="watches">0</td>
                                            <td class="thumbnail"></td>
                                            <td class="timeoriginalestimate"></td>
                                            <td class="timeestimate"></td>
                                            <td class="timespent"></td>
                                            <td class="workratio">&nbsp;
</td>
                                            <td class="subtasks">                </td>
                                            <td class="issuelinks">                </td>
                                            <td class="environment"></td>
                                            <td class="description">      When using WS-RM and MTOM, the generated message content is:<br/>
<br/>
POST /services/SayHello HTTP/1.1<br/>
<br/>
Content-Type: multipart/related; type=&quot;application/xop+xml&quot;; boundary=&quot;uuid:d861ffd6-2559-491d-b995-4420ac2e99e0&quot;; start=&quot;&lt;root.message@cxf.apache.org&gt;&quot;; start-info=&quot;application/soap+xml&quot;<br/>
<br/>
Accept: */*<br/>
<br/>
User-Agent: Apache CXF 2.2.2<br/>
<br/>
Cache-Control: no-cache<br/>
<br/>
Pragma: no-cache<br/>
<br/>
Host: localhost:12345<br/>
<br/>
Connection: keep-alive<br/>
<br/>
Content-Length: 1619<br/>
<br/>
<br/>
<br/>
<br/>
<br/>
--uuid:d861ffd6-2559-491d-b995-4420ac2e99e0<br/>
<br/>
Content-Type: application/xop+xml; charset=UTF-8; type=&quot;application/soap+xml&quot;;<br/>
<br/>
Content-Transfer-Encoding: binary<br/>
<br/>
Content-ID: &lt;root.message@cxf.apache.org&gt;<br/>
<br/>
<br/>
<br/>
<br/>
<br/>
--uuid:d861ffd6-2559-491d-b995-4420ac2e99e0<br/>
<br/>
Content-Type: application/octet-stream<br/>
<br/>
Content-Transfer-Encoding: binary<br/>
<br/>
Content-ID: &lt;d027f743-11a2-45e8-b95e-592f8b751bb4-1@http://cxf.apache.org/&gt;<br/>
<br/>
<br/>
<br/>
attachment content<br/>
<br/>
--uuid:d861ffd6-2559-491d-b995-4420ac2e99e0--&lt;soap:Envelope xmlns:soap=&quot;http://www.w3.org/2003/05/soap-envelope&quot;&gt;&lt;soap:Header&gt;&lt;Action xmlns=&quot;http://schemas.xmlsoap.org/ws/2004/08/addressing&quot;&gt;http://example.com/sayHello/ISayHello/hello&lt;/Action&gt;&lt;MessageID xmlns=&quot;http://schemas.xmlsoap.org/ws/2004/08/addressing&quot;&gt;urn:uuid:a2a9917b-4579-4945-aa38-e0da657dbbb4&lt;/MessageID&gt;&lt;To xmlns=&quot;http://schemas.xmlsoap.org/ws/2004/08/addressing&quot;&gt;http://localhost:12345/services/SayHello&lt;/To&gt;&lt;ReplyTo xmlns=&quot;http://schemas.xmlsoap.org/ws/2004/08/addressing&quot;&gt;&lt;Address&gt;http://schemas.xmlsoap.org/ws/2004/08/addressing/role/anonymous&lt;/Address&gt;&lt;/ReplyTo&gt;&lt;wsrm:Sequence xmlns:ns2=&quot;http://schemas.xmlsoap.org/ws/2004/08/addressing&quot; xmlns:wsrm=&quot;http://schemas.xmlsoap.org/ws/2005/02/rm&quot;&gt;&lt;wsrm:Identifier&gt;urn:uuid:b5383bf0-2444-4af8-b923-146d02610ab5&lt;/wsrm:Identifier&gt;&lt;wsrm:MessageNumber&gt;1&lt;/wsrm:MessageNumber&gt;&lt;/wsrm:Sequence&gt;&lt;/soap:Header&gt;&lt;soap:Body&gt;&lt;ns1:hello xmlns:ns1=&quot;http://example.com/sayHello&quot;&gt;&lt;arg0&gt;john&lt;/arg0&gt;&lt;arg1&gt;&lt;xop:Include xmlns:xop=&quot;http://www.w3.org/2004/08/xop/include&quot; href=&quot;cid:d027f743-11a2-45e8-b95e-592f8b751bb4-1@http%3A%2F%2Fcxf.apache.org%2F&quot;/&gt;&lt;/arg1&gt;&lt;/ns1:hello&gt;&lt;/soap:Body&gt;&lt;/soap:Envelope&gt;<br/>
<br/>
<br/>
<br/>
The soap envelope is sent after the last attachment instead of being in the &lt;root.message@cxf.apache.org&gt; part.<br/>
<br/>
This bug seems to be caused by :<br/>
1- the AttachmentOutInterceptor writes the prolog by using the current message outputstream (OS1)<br/>
2- the RetransmissionInterceptor wraps the message outputstream in a WriteOnCloseOutputStream (OS2)<br/>
3- the soap envelope is written in the current message outputsream OS2.<br/>
4- the attachments are written in the outputstream OS1 used to write the prolog.<br/>
5- the WriteOnCloseOutputstream OS2 is closed, and the soap envelope is appended in the wrapped outputstream OS1.<br/>
<br/>
<br/>
Setting the RetransmissionInterceptor to be before AttachmentOutInterceptor in the interceptor chain seems to solve this issue.<br/>
<br/>

  </td>
                                            <td class="security"></td>
                                            <td class="progress">     
</td>
                                            <td class="aggregateprogress">     
</td>
                                            <td class="aggregatetimespent"></td>
                                            <td class="aggregatetimeestimate"></td>
