                <tr id="issuerow12431543" rel="12431543" data-issuekey="CXF-2362" class="issuerow">
                                            <td class="project">    CXF
</td>
                                            <td class="issuekey">

    <a class="issue-link" data-issue-key="CXF-2362" href="https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/CXF-2362">CXF-2362</a>
</td>
                                            <td class="summary"><p>
                AegisJSONProviderTest.testManyTags fails with the ibm jdk
    </p>
</td>
                                            <td class="issuetype"> Bug</td>
                                            <td class="status">
                Closed
    </td>
                                            <td class="priority">   Major
</td>
                                            <td class="resolution">    Fixed
</td>
                                            <td class="assignee">            Sergey Beryozkin
    </td>
                                            <td class="reporter">            Peter Jones
    </td>
                                            <td class="creator">            Peter Jones
    </td>
                                            <td class="created"> 27/Jul/09 22:09 </td>
                                            <td class="lastViewed"> &nbsp; </td>
                                            <td class="updated"> 03/Aug/09 20:07 </td>
                                            <td class="resolutiondate"> 28/Jul/09 09:42 </td>
                                            <td class="versions">    &nbsp;
</td>
                                            <td class="fixVersions">                        2.2.3,                     2.3            </td>
                                            <td class="components">    &nbsp;
</td>
                                            <td class="duedate">    &nbsp;
</td>
                                            <td class="votes">0</td>
                                            <td class="watches">0</td>
                                            <td class="thumbnail"></td>
                                            <td class="timeoriginalestimate"></td>
                                            <td class="timeestimate"></td>
                                            <td class="timespent"></td>
                                            <td class="workratio">&nbsp;
</td>
                                            <td class="subtasks">                </td>
                                            <td class="issuelinks">                </td>
                                            <td class="environment">      ibm jdk on linux or aix
  </td>
                                            <td class="description">      The AegisJSONProviderTest.testManyTags () fails when run with the ibm jdk.  It attempts to do a straight string comparison of the response, however, the order of the elements in the reponse is different on the ibm jdk than it is on the sun jdk.<br/>
<br/>
Expected:<br/>
&lt;...,{&quot;ns1.TagVO&quot;:{&quot;ns1.[group&quot;:&quot;b&quot;,&quot;ns1.name&quot;:&quot;a]&quot;}}]}]}&gt;<br/>
Was:<br/>
&lt;...,{&quot;ns1.TagVO&quot;:{&quot;ns1.[name&quot;:&quot;a&quot;,&quot;ns1.group&quot;:&quot;b]&quot;}}]}]}&gt;<br/>
<br/>
Specifying a propOrder in the XmlType annotation doesn&#39;t seem to work for this case (using aegis), so probably the best solution is to check for a different string when running with the ibm jdk.
  </td>
                                            <td class="security"></td>
                                            <td class="progress">     
</td>
