                                            <td class="issuelinks">                </td>
                                            <td class="environment"></td>
                                            <td class="description">      <br/>
The JMSDestination.getReplyToDestination only looks at the incoming message for a &quot;rebased&quot; reply to location or the actual JMS ReplyTo destination.   It doesn&#39;t use the configuration for the jndiReplyDestinationName or jmsReplyDestinationName settings from the config.   It should check the Message first for the settings, and if not found, use the config settings.<br/>

  </td>
