                <tr id="issuerow12432706" rel="12432706" data-issuekey="CXF-2387" class="issuerow">
                                            <td class="project">    CXF
</td>
                                            <td class="issuekey">

    <a class="issue-link" data-issue-key="CXF-2387" href="https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/CXF-2387">CXF-2387</a>
</td>
                                            <td class="summary"><p>
                CXF does not call ConduitSelector.complete() on the server side.
    </p>
</td>
                                            <td class="issuetype"> Improvement</td>
                                            <td class="status">
                Closed
    </td>
                                            <td class="priority">   Major
</td>
                                            <td class="resolution">    Fixed
</td>
                                            <td class="assignee">            Daniel Kulp
    </td>
                                            <td class="reporter">            Gyorgy Orban
    </td>
                                            <td class="creator">            Gyorgy Orban
    </td>
                                            <td class="created"> 10/Aug/09 17:10 </td>
                                            <td class="lastViewed"> &nbsp; </td>
                                            <td class="updated"> 11/Oct/10 14:57 </td>
                                            <td class="resolutiondate"> 05/May/10 17:56 </td>
                                            <td class="versions">    &nbsp;
</td>
                                            <td class="fixVersions">                        Invalid            </td>
                                            <td class="components">                        Core            </td>
                                            <td class="duedate">    &nbsp;
</td>
                                            <td class="votes">0</td>
                                            <td class="watches">0</td>
                                            <td class="thumbnail"></td>
                                            <td class="timeoriginalestimate"></td>
                                            <td class="timeestimate"></td>
                                            <td class="timespent"></td>
                                            <td class="workratio">&nbsp;
</td>
                                            <td class="subtasks">                </td>
                                            <td class="issuelinks">                </td>
                                            <td class="environment"></td>
                                            <td class="description">      I guess the main reason for it is that closing the input stream in a servlet is usually not a good idea. As the default implementation in PreexistingConduitSelector.complete() closes the input stream of the request message, it would cause problems when CXF is deployed in Jetty or in other servlet containers. On the other hand, from design and extensibility perspective it would be quite useful to call ConduitSelector.complete() similarly to the client side for the following reasons:<br/>
<br/>
* integration with other transports could make use of such a lifecycle callback<br/>
* If the request InputStream is wrapped (let&#39;s say we want to monitor throughput or filter the inputstream for some reason) it is quite difficult to catch the end of the stream without a close() callback on the InputStream. If complete() was called, a custom ConduitSelector could solve that.<br/>
<br/>
I think ConduitSelector.complete() could be included in the Destination implementations.<br/>
Could you please give your opinion on this?
  </td>
                                            <td class="security"></td>
                                            <td class="progress">     
</td>
                                            <td class="aggregateprogress">     
</td>
                                            <td class="aggregatetimespent"></td>
                                            <td class="aggregatetimeestimate"></td>
                                            <td class="aggregatetimeoriginalestimate"></td>
                                            <td class="labels">    </td>
