</td>
                                            <td class="subtasks">                </td>
                                            <td class="issuelinks">                </td>
                                            <td class="environment"></td>
                                            <td class="description">      org.apache.cxf.jaxrs.provider.AegisJSONProviderTest.testWriteCollection() will explode if you un-ignore it. Why?<br/>
<br/>
org.apache.cxf.jaxrs.provider.AegisElementProvider.createStreamWriter(Class&lt;?&gt;, OutputStream) is called with a Class, but it needs a full java.lang.reflect.Type to work right. org.apache.cxf.jaxrs.provider.AegisJSONProvider.createStreamWriter(Class&lt;?&gt;, OutputStream) wants to map the type to a QName, and that won&#39;t work for generic types and collections from a plain class.<br/>
<br/>

  </td>
