</td>
                                            <td class="subtasks">                </td>
                                            <td class="issuelinks">                </td>
                                            <td class="environment"></td>
                                            <td class="description">      After injecting the the HttpServletResponse with the @Context annotation:<br/>
<br/>
    @POST<br/>
    @Path(&quot;/login&quot;)<br/>
    public Feed login(@FormParam(&quot;username&quot;) String username,<br/>
            @FormParam(&quot;password&quot;) String password,<br/>
            @Context HttpServletResponse httpServletResponse) <br/>
<br/>
and than setting a status code (for example 401 if the user is not authorized), the status code get lost.<br/>
<br/>
See here for workarounds and more detials:<br/>
http://www.nabble.com/Setting-the-status-code-in-the-injected-(via-the-jax-rs-@context)--HttpServletResponse-td25883621.html
