                <tr id="issuerow12439220" rel="12439220" data-issuekey="CXF-2502" class="issuerow">
                                            <td class="project">    CXF
</td>
                                            <td class="issuekey">

    <a class="issue-link" data-issue-key="CXF-2502" href="https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/CXF-2502">CXF-2502</a>
</td>
                                            <td class="summary"><p>
                decoupled WS-A and WS-Sec does not result in faults back to clients
    </p>
</td>
                                            <td class="issuetype"> Bug</td>
                                            <td class="status">
                Closed
    </td>
                                            <td class="priority">   Major
</td>
                                            <td class="resolution">    Fixed
</td>
                                            <td class="assignee">            Daniel Kulp
    </td>
                                            <td class="reporter">            Daniel Kulp
    </td>
                                            <td class="creator">            Daniel Kulp
    </td>
                                            <td class="created"> 27/Oct/09 21:06 </td>
                                            <td class="lastViewed"> &nbsp; </td>
                                            <td class="updated"> 04/Dec/09 22:34 </td>
                                            <td class="resolutiondate"> 28/Oct/09 13:37 </td>
                                            <td class="versions">                        2.2.4            </td>
                                            <td class="fixVersions">                        2.2.5            </td>
                                            <td class="components">                        WS-* Components            </td>
                                            <td class="duedate">    &nbsp;
</td>
                                            <td class="votes">0</td>
                                            <td class="watches">0</td>
                                            <td class="thumbnail"></td>
                                            <td class="timeoriginalestimate"></td>
                                            <td class="timeestimate"></td>
                                            <td class="timespent"></td>
                                            <td class="workratio">&nbsp;
</td>
                                            <td class="subtasks">                </td>
                                            <td class="issuelinks">                                        CXF-2489                        </td>
                                            <td class="environment"></td>
                                            <td class="description">      <br/>
The example in:<br/>
https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/CXF-2489<br/>
shows this.<br/>
<br/>
Basically, if an interceptor that lives between MAPCodec and MAPAggregator throws an exception, the fault is sent like a normal response.  However, the client is looking for a partial response and then the fault on the decoupled channel.   Thus, the client never sees the fault and just gets an IOException and/or hangs.<br/>
<br/>

  </td>
