                                            <td class="subtasks">                </td>
                                            <td class="issuelinks">                </td>
                                            <td class="environment"></td>
                                            <td class="description">      A client makes a String greetMe(String) invocation against a backend server. Because of a problem in the server, it resonds with a SOAP message corresponding to a String sayHi() response. The client processes the response without an error. Here is the schema for the response elements for the two invocations:<br/>
           &lt;element name=&quot;sayHi&quot;&gt;<br/>
                &lt;complexType/&gt;<br/>
            &lt;/element&gt;<br/>
            &lt;element name=&quot;sayHiResponse&quot;&gt;<br/>
                &lt;complexType&gt;<br/>
                    &lt;sequence&gt;<br/>
                        &lt;element name=&quot;responseType&quot; type=&quot;string&quot;/&gt;<br/>
                    &lt;/sequence&gt;<br/>
                &lt;/complexType&gt;<br/>
            &lt;/element&gt;<br/>
            &lt;element name=&quot;greetMe&quot;&gt;<br/>
                &lt;complexType&gt;<br/>
                    &lt;sequence&gt;<br/>
                        &lt;element name=&quot;requestType&quot; type=&quot;tns:MyStringType&quot;/&gt;<br/>
                    &lt;/sequence&gt;<br/>
                &lt;/complexType&gt;<br/>
            &lt;/element&gt;<br/>
            &lt;element name=&quot;greetMeResponse&quot;&gt;<br/>
                &lt;complexType&gt;<br/>
                    &lt;sequence&gt;<br/>
                        &lt;element name=&quot;responseType&quot; type=&quot;string&quot;/&gt;<br/>
                    &lt;/sequence&gt;<br/>
                &lt;/complexType&gt;<br/>
            &lt;/element&gt;<br/>
<br/>
In discussions with Dan, he suggested that because the child elements of both the sayHiResponse and the greetMeResonse are the same, then it is quite possible that sayHiResponse would be accepted in place of a greetMeResponse.
  </td>
