                                            <td class="environment">      Spring 2.5.6
  </td>
                                            <td class="description">      In some cases we&#39;re using the ContextSingletonBeanFactoryLocator to obtain a cxf client from a non spring bean (cp. Spring&#39;s section about &quot;Glue code and the evil singleton&quot;). For example:<br/>
BeanFactory bf = ContextSingletonBeanFactoryLocator.getInstance().useBeanFactory(&quot;cssBeanFactory&quot;).getFactory();<br/>
final AccountService accountService = (AccountService) bf.getBean(&quot;accountService&quot;, AccountService.class);<br/>
<br/>
With 2.2.3 this was no problem...the proxies were only created once at startup (no further call, when bf.getBean is called):<br/>
	ReflectionServiceFactoryBean.buildServiceFromClass() line: 351	<br/>
	ReflectionServiceFactoryBean.initializeServiceModel() line: 444	<br/>
