                <tr id="issuerow12444686" rel="12444686" data-issuekey="CXF-2601" class="issuerow">
                                            <td class="project">    CXF
</td>
                                            <td class="issuekey">

    <a class="issue-link" data-issue-key="CXF-2601" href="https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/CXF-2601">CXF-2601</a>
</td>
                                            <td class="summary"><p>
                Faults generated with XMLBeans binding are not wrapped correctly
    </p>
</td>
                                            <td class="issuetype"> Bug</td>
                                            <td class="status">
                Closed
    </td>
                                            <td class="priority">   Major
</td>
                                            <td class="resolution">    Fixed
</td>
                                            <td class="assignee">            Daniel Kulp
    </td>
                                            <td class="reporter">            Martin Murphy
    </td>
                                            <td class="creator">            Martin Murphy
    </td>
                                            <td class="created"> 05/Jan/10 10:58 </td>
                                            <td class="lastViewed"> &nbsp; </td>
                                            <td class="updated"> 01/Feb/10 19:02 </td>
                                            <td class="resolutiondate"> 05/Jan/10 22:46 </td>
                                            <td class="versions">                        2.2.5            </td>
                                            <td class="fixVersions">                        2.1.9,                     2.2.6            </td>
                                            <td class="components">    &nbsp;
</td>
                                            <td class="duedate">    &nbsp;
</td>
                                            <td class="votes">0</td>
                                            <td class="watches">0</td>
                                            <td class="thumbnail"></td>
                                            <td class="timeoriginalestimate"></td>
                                            <td class="timeestimate"></td>
                                            <td class="timespent"></td>
                                            <td class="workratio">&nbsp;
</td>
                                            <td class="subtasks">                </td>
                                            <td class="issuelinks">                </td>
                                            <td class="environment">      Tested on windows with JDK jdk1.5.0_18
  </td>
                                            <td class="description">      When Fault in WSDL is defined as simple String and XMLBeans binding is used, then the fault is marshaled in a way, that doesn&#39;t allow proper unmarshalling of the Exception on the client side. Example fault looks like<br/>
<br/>
{code:xml}<br/>
&lt;soap:Envelope xmlns:soap=&quot;http://schemas.xmlsoap.org/soap/envelope/&quot;&gt;<br/>
  &lt;soap:Body&gt;<br/>
    &lt;soap:Fault&gt;<br/>
      &lt;faultcode&gt;soap:Server&lt;/faultcode&gt;<br/>
      &lt;faultstring&gt;message&lt;/faultstring&gt;<br/>
      &lt;detail&gt;detail&lt;/detail&gt;<br/>
    &lt;/soap:Fault&gt;<br/>
  &lt;/soap:Body&gt;<br/>
&lt;/soap:Envelope&gt;<br/>
{code}<br/>
<br/>
As you can see detail doesn&#39;t have any information about fault type. This means that the exception cannot be mapped to the appropriate type
  </td>
