</td>
                                            <td class="subtasks">                </td>
                                            <td class="issuelinks">                </td>
                                            <td class="environment"></td>
                                            <td class="description">      Using the -autoNameResolution option in WSDLToJava produces inconsistent results in the naming of classes for the same wsdl. Specifically, on one developer machine, it names one class GetMemberCHResponse and another GetMemberCHResponse2, but for another developer, these classes are reversed such that GetMemberCHResponse = GetMemberCHResponse2 and vice versa for developer #2. This is a problem when trying to interact with the stub code from the application code.
  </td>
