                <tr id="issuerow12456335" rel="12456335" data-issuekey="CXF-2674" class="issuerow">
                                            <td class="project">    CXF
</td>
                                            <td class="issuekey">

    <a class="issue-link" data-issue-key="CXF-2674" href="https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/CXF-2674">CXF-2674</a>
</td>
                                            <td class="summary"><p>
                @Resource not injecting WebServiceContext in jaxws intereceptor
    </p>
</td>
                                            <td class="issuetype"> Bug</td>
                                            <td class="status">
                Closed
    </td>
                                            <td class="priority">   Major
</td>
                                            <td class="resolution">    Not A Problem
</td>
                                            <td class="assignee">            Daniel Kulp
    </td>
                                            <td class="reporter">            Auke Noppe
    </td>
                                            <td class="creator">            Auke Noppe
    </td>
                                            <td class="created"> 15/Feb/10 15:38 </td>
                                            <td class="lastViewed"> &nbsp; </td>
                                            <td class="updated"> 11/Oct/10 14:48 </td>
                                            <td class="resolutiondate"> 09/Mar/10 00:29 </td>
                                            <td class="versions">                        2.2.5            </td>
                                            <td class="fixVersions">                        Invalid            </td>
                                            <td class="components">    &nbsp;
</td>
                                            <td class="duedate">    &nbsp;
</td>
                                            <td class="votes">0</td>
                                            <td class="watches">0</td>
                                            <td class="thumbnail"></td>
                                            <td class="timeoriginalestimate"></td>
                                            <td class="timeestimate"></td>
                                            <td class="timespent"></td>
                                            <td class="workratio">&nbsp;
</td>
                                            <td class="subtasks">                </td>
                                            <td class="issuelinks">                </td>
                                            <td class="environment">      tomcat 6.0.18, Spring 2.5, Spring Security 2.0.5, cxf-2.2.5 with wss4j-1.5.8
  </td>
                                            <td class="description">      If you want to inject the WebServiceContext into a In/Out-Interceptor configured with xml (e.g. &lt;jaxws:ininterceptors&gt;&lt;bean id=&quot;someInterceptor&quot; class=&quot;test.SomeInterceptor&quot;/&gt;&lt;/jaxws:ininterceptors /&gt;) with the @resource annotation, the WebServiceContext is null. (Even with component-scan enabled and annotation-config defined)<br/>
<br/>
If you inject the WebServiceContext into the interceptor with a property-setter in the xml (e.g. &lt;property name=&quot;ctx&quot; value=&quot;javax.xml.ws.WebServiceContext&quot; /&gt;) the instance is not empty, but holding nothing (like MessageContext )<br/>
<br/>
The documentation suggest the way with the @Resource annotation, so this is rather confusing.<br/>
<br/>
The work-around I found, is to set the properties I wanted to set on the message in the handleMessage method of the interceptor (e.g. message.put(&quot;someKey&quot;, someValue); )<br/>
I would rather see the @Resource injection working.<br/>
<br/>
Regards,<br/>
<br/>
Auke Noppe<br/>
Developer @ Ymor (.nl)
  </td>
