                                            <td class="timeestimate"></td>
                                            <td class="timespent"></td>
                                            <td class="workratio">&nbsp;
</td>
                                            <td class="subtasks">                </td>
                                            <td class="issuelinks">                </td>
                                            <td class="environment"></td>
                                            <td class="description">      current implementation from UriInfoImpl:<br/>
{code}<br/>
    public URI getRequestUri() {<br/>
        String path = getAbsolutePathAsString();<br/>
        String queries = (String)message.get(Message.QUERY_STRING);<br/>
        if (queries != null) {<br/>
            path += &quot;?&quot; + queries;<br/>
        }<br/>
        return URI.create(path);<br/>
    }<br/>
{code}<br/>
This fails for URIs that have characters that have to be escaped as of rfc2396. <br/>
<br/>
Examples: http://localhost:13080/services/rest/crypto/hash;algorithm=S{A/text/foo or http://localhost:13080/services/rest/crypto/hash;algorithm=S^A/text/foo<br/>
fail with Exception during getRequestUri() due to { or ^ as part of the uri<br/>

  </td>
