                <tr id="issuerow12456637" rel="12456637" data-issuekey="CXF-2680" class="issuerow">
                                            <td class="project">    CXF
</td>
                                            <td class="issuekey">

    <a class="issue-link" data-issue-key="CXF-2680" href="https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/CXF-2680">CXF-2680</a>
</td>
                                            <td class="summary"><p>
                wsdlvalidator ignores WSDL constraints on element order
    </p>
</td>
                                            <td class="issuetype"> Bug</td>
                                            <td class="status">
                Closed
    </td>
                                            <td class="priority">   Major
</td>
                                            <td class="resolution">    Not A Problem
</td>
                                            <td class="assignee">    <em>Unassigned</em>
</td>
                                            <td class="reporter">            Dennis Sosnoski
    </td>
                                            <td class="creator">            Dennis Sosnoski
    </td>
                                            <td class="created"> 18/Feb/10 10:45 </td>
                                            <td class="lastViewed"> &nbsp; </td>
                                            <td class="updated"> 19/Feb/10 02:46 </td>
                                            <td class="resolutiondate"> 19/Feb/10 01:05 </td>
                                            <td class="versions">                        2.2.5            </td>
                                            <td class="fixVersions">    &nbsp;
</td>
                                            <td class="components">                        Tooling            </td>
                                            <td class="duedate">    &nbsp;
</td>
                                            <td class="votes">0</td>
                                            <td class="watches">0</td>
                                            <td class="thumbnail"></td>
                                            <td class="timeoriginalestimate"></td>
                                            <td class="timeestimate"></td>
                                            <td class="timespent"></td>
                                            <td class="workratio">&nbsp;
</td>
                                            <td class="subtasks">                </td>
                                            <td class="issuelinks">                </td>
                                            <td class="environment"></td>
                                            <td class="description">      When running WSDLToJava with the -validate flag a WSDL with elements in incorrect order is accepted without complaint. In the example tested, the wsdl:service element precedes the wsdl:types element. This is a violation of the WSDL 1.1 schema definition, which defines the wsdl:definitions element structure as:<br/>
<br/>
   &lt;complexType name=&quot;definitionsType&quot;&gt;<br/>
      &lt;complexContent&gt;<br/>
         &lt;extension base=&quot;wsdl:documented&quot;&gt;<br/>
            &lt;sequence&gt;<br/>
               &lt;element ref=&quot;wsdl:import&quot; minOccurs=&quot;0&quot; maxOccurs=&quot;unbounded&quot;/&gt;<br/>
               &lt;element ref=&quot;wsdl:types&quot; minOccurs=&quot;0&quot;/&gt;<br/>
               &lt;element ref=&quot;wsdl:message&quot; minOccurs=&quot;0&quot; maxOccurs=&quot;unbounded&quot;/&gt;<br/>
               &lt;element ref=&quot;wsdl:portType&quot; minOccurs=&quot;0&quot; maxOccurs=&quot;unbounded&quot;/&gt;<br/>
               &lt;element ref=&quot;wsdl:binding&quot; minOccurs=&quot;0&quot; maxOccurs=&quot;unbounded&quot;/&gt;<br/>
               &lt;element ref=&quot;wsdl:service&quot; minOccurs=&quot;0&quot; maxOccurs=&quot;unbounded&quot;/&gt;<br/>
               &lt;any namespace=&quot;##other&quot; minOccurs=&quot;0&quot; maxOccurs=&quot;unbounded&quot;&gt;<br/>
                  &lt;annotation&gt;<br/>
                     &lt;documentation&gt;to support extensibility elements &lt;/documentation&gt;<br/>
                  &lt;/annotation&gt;<br/>
               &lt;/any&gt;<br/>
            &lt;/sequence&gt;<br/>
            &lt;attribute name=&quot;targetNamespace&quot; type=&quot;uriReference&quot; use=&quot;optional&quot;/&gt;<br/>
            &lt;attribute name=&quot;name&quot; type=&quot;NMTOKEN&quot; use=&quot;optional&quot;/&gt;<br/>
         &lt;/extension&gt;<br/>
      &lt;/complexContent&gt;<br/>
  &lt;/complexType&gt;<br/>
<br/>
If there&#39;s going to be a -validate flag it should perform a proper validation of the WSDL. I realize it&#39;s common for implementations to accept invalid WSDL of this type, but there should at least be a warning generated so that users will realize their WSDL is not actually valid.
  </td>
                                            <td class="security"></td>
                                            <td class="progress">     
</td>
