                                            <td class="creator">            Stéphane Landelle
    </td>
                                            <td class="created"> 26/Feb/10 16:43 </td>
                                            <td class="lastViewed"> &nbsp; </td>
                                            <td class="updated"> 08/Aug/11 18:19 </td>
                                            <td class="resolutiondate"> 25/May/11 18:51 </td>
                                            <td class="versions">                        2.2.6            </td>
                                            <td class="fixVersions">                        Invalid            </td>
                                            <td class="components">                        Documentation            </td>
                                            <td class="duedate">    &nbsp;
</td>
                                            <td class="votes">0</td>
                                            <td class="watches">0</td>
                                            <td class="thumbnail"></td>
                                            <td class="timeoriginalestimate"></td>
                                            <td class="timeestimate"></td>
                                            <td class="timespent"></td>
                                            <td class="workratio">&nbsp;
</td>
                                            <td class="subtasks">                </td>
                                            <td class="issuelinks">                </td>
                                            <td class="environment">      Windows XP and AIX<br/>
WAS 6.1.0.27 (no WS feature pack) 
  </td>
                                            <td class="description">      I don&#39;t know if creating an issue is the right thing to do or if I should just post on the mailing list.<br/>
Sorry if I&#39;m wrong.<br/>
<br/>
I tried to deploy CXF 2.2.6 on WAS 6.1.0.27 (no WS feature pack) with the configuration detailed in the user guide, but it wouldn&#39;t work and I still got CNFE on javax.xml.transform.stax.StAXResult.<br/>
<br/>
I finally managed to deploy successfully with the following configuration (much simplier than the one in the user guide) :<br/>
<br/>
1) have jaxp-api and jaxp-ri inside the WAR (check you don&#39;t have any double, such as jsr173_api, stax-api or geronimo-stax-api)<br/>
2) create a shared lib with wsdl4j<br/>
3) create a classloader on the server with this shared lib, set as PARENT_LAST<br/>
4) configure the WAR classloader as PARENT_LAST<br/>
<br/>
If this configuration is confirmed, the user guide should be updated.<br/>
<br/>
Sincerely,<br/>
<br/>
Stephane Landelle
  </td>
