</td>
                                            <td class="subtasks">                </td>
                                            <td class="issuelinks">                </td>
                                            <td class="environment"></td>
                                            <td class="description">      The class org.apache.cxf.binding.soap.interceptor.Soap12FaultOutInterceptor.Soap12FaultOutInterceptorInternal uses java.util.Locale#getDisplayLanguage() for determining the value of the xml:lang attribute of the SOAP Text Element. To get a language code, the proper method should be java.util.Locale#getLanguage().<br/>
<br/>
If this is fixed, you can set your default locale language to the xml:lang attribute by creating a non-empty resource &#39;org/apache/cxf/binding/soap/interceptor/Messages_&lt;language code&gt;.properties&#39; in the classpath. Currently there is no way to set the value other than &#39;en&#39; (default value).<br/>

  </td>
