                                            <td class="description">      Assuming you have split out XSDs into their own project, and you have an endpoint configured like so:<br/>
<br/>
{code}<br/>
        &lt;jaxws:properties&gt;<br/>
            &lt;entry key=&quot;schema-validation-enabled&quot;<br/>
                   value=&quot;true&quot;/&gt;<br/>
        &lt;/jaxws:properties&gt;<br/>
{code}<br/>
<br/>
What happens is, if you send a request to your endpoint it can&#39;t find the referenced XSDs.<br/>
<br/>
The error message I get differs on whether I use 2.2.6 or 2.2.7-SNAPSHOT.  I&#39;m not sure if they both represent the same problem.  In 2.2.6, the problem states that the WSDL had a &quot;premature end of file&quot;, but when I debugged I found it was simply the fact the schemas it references could not be found:   <br/>
<br/>
{code:title=2.2.6 error}<br/>
