                                            <td class="watches">0</td>
                                            <td class="thumbnail"></td>
                                            <td class="timeoriginalestimate"></td>
                                            <td class="timeestimate"></td>
                                            <td class="timespent"></td>
                                            <td class="workratio">&nbsp;
</td>
                                            <td class="subtasks">                </td>
                                            <td class="issuelinks">                </td>
                                            <td class="environment">      Windows XP
  </td>
                                            <td class="description">      If I have a WSDL that imports a schema from a relation path such as below, it does not work in Windows.  <br/>
{code}<br/>
		&lt;xsd:schema xmlns:xsd=&quot;http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema&quot;&gt;<br/>
			&lt;xsd:import namespace=&quot;urn:RelPath&quot; schemaLocation=&quot;../schemas/configuration/bar.xsd&quot;&gt;<br/>
			&lt;/xsd:import&gt;<br/>
		&lt;/xsd:schema&gt;<br/>
{code}<br/>
<br/>
It is because of two issues in org.apache.cxf.resource.URIResolver.<br/>
<br/>
1) URIResolver checks for baseUriStr.startsWith(&quot;file:/&quot;) but Windows file URI could be &quot;file:C:/foo/bar&quot;<br/>
<br/>
2) URIResolver would include fragment (e.g. #type2) as file path when creates a File object.  This is not showing up as a problem in UNIX machines because &quot;new URI(baseUriStr)&quot; is able to parse the baseUriStr correctly.<br/>

  </td>
