                <tr id="issuerow12462028" rel="12462028" data-issuekey="CXF-2764" class="issuerow">
                                            <td class="project">    CXF
</td>
                                            <td class="issuekey">

    <a class="issue-link" data-issue-key="CXF-2764" href="https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/CXF-2764">CXF-2764</a>
</td>
                                            <td class="summary"><p>
                CXF Client Side Duplication of targetnamespace
    </p>
</td>
                                            <td class="issuetype"> Bug</td>
                                            <td class="status">
                Closed
    </td>
                                            <td class="priority">   Major
</td>
                                            <td class="resolution">    Cannot Reproduce
</td>
                                            <td class="assignee">    <em>Unassigned</em>
</td>
                                            <td class="reporter">            Seamus Loftus
    </td>
                                            <td class="creator">            Seamus Loftus
    </td>
                                            <td class="created"> 14/Apr/10 11:41 </td>
                                            <td class="lastViewed"> &nbsp; </td>
                                            <td class="updated"> 18/Apr/11 12:44 </td>
                                            <td class="resolutiondate"> 11/Apr/11 13:16 </td>
                                            <td class="versions">                        2.2.7            </td>
                                            <td class="fixVersions">                        Invalid            </td>
                                            <td class="components">                        JAX-WS Runtime            </td>
                                            <td class="duedate">    &nbsp;
</td>
                                            <td class="votes">0</td>
                                            <td class="watches">0</td>
                                            <td class="thumbnail"></td>
                                            <td class="timeoriginalestimate"></td>
                                            <td class="timeestimate"></td>
                                            <td class="timespent"></td>
                                            <td class="workratio">&nbsp;
</td>
                                            <td class="subtasks">                </td>
                                            <td class="issuelinks">                </td>
                                            <td class="environment">      Windows XP
  </td>
                                            <td class="description">      I am hosting a webservice and a webapp on the same server, generated from wsdl2java. I can contact the service just fine through SoapUI and it returns a single namespace declaration when posted to the live server on AIX, but when I am working locally and use SoapUI it generates two instances of xlmns=&quot;&quot; instead of a single one in my xml. I have copied below an example xml file:<br/>
<br/>
&lt;soap:Envelope xmlns:soap=&quot;http://schemas.xmlsoap.org/soap/envelope/&quot;&gt;&lt;soap:Body&gt; <br/>
&lt;SendResponse xmlns=&quot;http://myendpoint.org/service&quot; xmlns:ns2=&quot;http://docs.oasis-open.org/wss/2004/01/oasis-200401-wss-wssecurity-secext-1.0.xsd&quot;&gt; <br/>
&lt;Receipt&gt; <br/>
&lt;MyReceipt xmlns:ns3=&quot;http://myendpoint.org/service&quot; xmlns=&quot;&quot; xmlns=&quot;&quot; xmlns:ns6=&quot;http://myapp.myserver.net/myservicegroup/myservice/V01&quot; receiptVersion=&quot;V01&quot;&gt; <br/>
  &lt;ReceiptHeader&gt; <br/>
    &lt;ReceiptTimestamp&gt;2010-04-13T08:27:03.036-04:00&lt;/ReceiptTimestamp&gt; <br/>
  &lt;/ReceiptHeader&gt; <br/>
  &lt;TransmissionReceipt&gt; <br/>
    &lt;TransmissionID&gt;testuser&lt;/TransmissionID&gt; <br/>
    &lt;TransmissionTimestamp&gt;2010-04-13T08:27:03.036-04:00&lt;/TransmissionTimestamp&gt; <br/>
  &lt;/TransmissionReceipt&gt; <br/>
&lt;/MyReceipt&gt;&lt;/Receipt&gt;&lt;/SendResponse&gt;&lt;/soap:Body&gt;&lt;/soap:Envelope&gt; <br/>
<br/>
So when it unmarshalls, it fails badly when I use my webapp as a webservice client. Why is CXF adding a second namespace? I watched the debug all the way through until the return and it looked 100% perfect on the webservice side, no duplicate name space at all. It does not happen until the return of the xml to the client side.<br/>

  </td>
