                <tr id="issuerow12472608" rel="12472608" data-issuekey="CXF-2961" class="issuerow">
                                            <td class="project">    CXF
</td>
                                            <td class="issuekey">

    <a class="issue-link" data-issue-key="CXF-2961" href="https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/CXF-2961">CXF-2961</a>
</td>
                                            <td class="summary"><p>
                JAXRS Web Client pre-connect errors can be better propagated
    </p>
</td>
                                            <td class="issuetype"> Bug</td>
                                            <td class="status">
                Closed
    </td>
                                            <td class="priority">   Minor
</td>
                                            <td class="resolution">    Fixed
</td>
                                            <td class="assignee">            Sergey Beryozkin
    </td>
                                            <td class="reporter">            Peter Easton
    </td>
                                            <td class="creator">            Peter Easton
    </td>
                                            <td class="created"> 26/Aug/10 15:23 </td>
                                            <td class="lastViewed"> &nbsp; </td>
                                            <td class="updated"> 11/Oct/10 14:45 </td>
                                            <td class="resolutiondate"> 31/Aug/10 20:58 </td>
                                            <td class="versions">                        2.2.10,                     2.3            </td>
                                            <td class="fixVersions">                        2.3,                     2.2.11            </td>
                                            <td class="components">                        JAX-RS            </td>
                                            <td class="duedate">    &nbsp;
</td>
                                            <td class="votes">0</td>
                                            <td class="watches">0</td>
                                            <td class="thumbnail"></td>
                                            <td class="timeoriginalestimate"></td>
                                            <td class="timeestimate"></td>
                                            <td class="timespent"></td>
                                            <td class="workratio">&nbsp;
</td>
                                            <td class="subtasks">                </td>
                                            <td class="issuelinks">                </td>
                                            <td class="environment"></td>
                                            <td class="description">      HTTP client errors fall into 2 categories:<br/>
<br/>
i. The connect succeeds, a  non-2xx HTTP response is returned by the service.<br/>
ii. The connect does not succeed because of local HTTP client runtime issues (bad hostname, port unavailable, unsupported method).<br/>
In the later error cases a WebApplication exceptions is returned BUT no root cause exception is available.<br/>
<br/>
A suggested patch is included.<br/>

  </td>
                                            <td class="security"></td>
                                            <td class="progress">     
</td>
                                            <td class="aggregateprogress">     
</td>
                                            <td class="aggregatetimespent"></td>
                                            <td class="aggregatetimeestimate"></td>
                                            <td class="aggregatetimeoriginalestimate"></td>
                                            <td class="labels">    </td>
                                            <td class="customfield_12310060"></td>
                                            <td class="customfield_12310220">            <span title="26/Aug/10 21:47"><time class="livestamp allow-future" datetime="2010-08-26T21:47:07+0000">26/Aug/10 9:47 PM</time></span>
