                <tr id="issuerow12472744" rel="12472744" data-issuekey="CXF-2963" class="issuerow">
                                            <td class="project">    CXF
</td>
                                            <td class="issuekey">

    <a class="issue-link" data-issue-key="CXF-2963" href="https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/CXF-2963">CXF-2963</a>
</td>
                                            <td class="summary"><p>
                Signature coverage of signed XML Encryption elements created using standard WSS4J elements cannot be verified with WS-SP configuration or the CryptoCoverageChecker
    </p>
</td>
                                            <td class="issuetype"> Bug</td>
                                            <td class="status">
                Closed
    </td>
                                            <td class="priority">   Minor
</td>
                                            <td class="resolution">    Fixed
</td>
                                            <td class="assignee">            David Valeri
    </td>
                                            <td class="reporter">            David Valeri
    </td>
                                            <td class="creator">            David Valeri
    </td>
                                            <td class="created"> 27/Aug/10 21:00 </td>
                                            <td class="lastViewed"> &nbsp; </td>
                                            <td class="updated"> 11/Oct/10 14:46 </td>
                                            <td class="resolutiondate"> 01/Sep/10 19:51 </td>
                                            <td class="versions">                        2.2.10,                     2.3            </td>
                                            <td class="fixVersions">                        2.3,                     2.2.11            </td>
                                            <td class="components">                        WS-* Components            </td>
                                            <td class="duedate">    &nbsp;
</td>
                                            <td class="votes">0</td>
                                            <td class="watches">0</td>
                                            <td class="thumbnail"></td>
                                            <td class="timeoriginalestimate"></td>
                                            <td class="timeestimate"></td>
                                            <td class="timespent"></td>
                                            <td class="workratio">&nbsp;
</td>
                                            <td class="subtasks">                </td>
                                            <td class="issuelinks">                                        WSS-242                        </td>
                                            <td class="environment"></td>
                                            <td class="description">      When using manual configuration of WSS4J on the client outbound interceptor chain, the resulting message contains extraneous Id attributes on the signed XML Encryption elements.  The signature is computed using a different attribute value than that reported by the encryption results from WSS4J on the server side.<br/>
<br/>
For instance, the following signed element is referenced in different ways:<br/>
<br/>
&lt;xenc:EncryptedData xmlns:wsu=&quot;http://docs.oasis-open.org/wss/2004/01/oasis-200401-wss-wssecurity-utility-1.0.xsd&quot; xmlns:xenc=&quot;http://www.w3.org/2001/04/xmlenc#&quot; Id=&quot;EncDataId-659&quot; Type=&quot;http://www.w3.org/2001/04/xmlenc#Element&quot; wsu:Id=&quot;id-663&quot;&gt;<br/>
<br/>
Signature: &lt;ds:Reference URI=&quot;#id-663&quot;&gt;<br/>
Encryption: &lt;xenc:DataReference URI=&quot;#EncDataId-659&quot; /&gt;<br/>
<br/>
The extra ID invalidates the XML Encryption schema and troubles the logic that determines signed encrypted content.
  </td>
