                <tr id="issuerow12473249" rel="12473249" data-issuekey="CXF-2972" class="issuerow">
                                            <td class="project">    CXF
</td>
                                            <td class="issuekey">

    <a class="issue-link" data-issue-key="CXF-2972" href="https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/CXF-2972">CXF-2972</a>
</td>
                                            <td class="summary"><p>
                MapAggregator should throw a fault when ReplyTo address is set to None in case of two-way requests 
    </p>
</td>
                                            <td class="issuetype"> Bug</td>
                                            <td class="status">
                Closed
    </td>
                                            <td class="priority">   Major
</td>
                                            <td class="resolution">    Fixed
</td>
                                            <td class="assignee">            Sergey Beryozkin
    </td>
                                            <td class="reporter">            Sergey Beryozkin
    </td>
                                            <td class="creator">            Sergey Beryozkin
    </td>
                                            <td class="created"> 03/Sep/10 15:56 </td>
                                            <td class="lastViewed"> &nbsp; </td>
                                            <td class="updated"> 11/Oct/10 14:46 </td>
                                            <td class="resolutiondate"> 05/Oct/10 16:00 </td>
                                            <td class="versions">                        2.2.10            </td>
                                            <td class="fixVersions">                        2.3,                     2.2.11            </td>
                                            <td class="components">                        WS-* Components            </td>
                                            <td class="duedate">    &nbsp;
</td>
                                            <td class="votes">0</td>
                                            <td class="watches">0</td>
                                            <td class="thumbnail"></td>
                                            <td class="timeoriginalestimate"></td>
                                            <td class="timeestimate"></td>
                                            <td class="timespent"></td>
                                            <td class="workratio">&nbsp;
</td>
                                            <td class="subtasks">                </td>
                                            <td class="issuelinks">                </td>
                                            <td class="environment"></td>
                                            <td class="description">      According to http://www.w3.org/TR/ws-addr-core/#eprinfomodel, when ReplyTo address is set to<br/>
&quot;http://www.w3.org/2005/08/addressing/none&quot;<br/>
<br/>
no reply message should be sent. Essentially, 202 is expected.<br/>
<br/>
Now, JAXWS TCK expects a fault instead. It probably does make sense indeed to reply with a fault because returning 202 for two requests does not make much sense<br/>
 
  </td>
