                                            <td class="environment"></td>
                                            <td class="description">      CXF sets a null collection, rather than an empty one, when the query param isn&#39;t in the request<br/>
<br/>
Example:<br/>
    @GET<br/>
    @Path(&quot;/stuff&quot;)<br/>
    public Response get(@QueryParam(&quot;option&quot;) Set&lt;String&gt; options) { ... }<br/>
<br/>
and http://localhost:8080/stuff is called (but ?option=abc is not on the query string), then options will be null, but it should be an empty Set<br/>
<br/>
The javadocs in @DefaultValue says:<br/>
If this annotation is not used and the corresponding metadata is not present in the request, the value will be an empty collection for List, Set or SortedSet<br/>
<br/>
this seems similar to CXF-1675
