                <tr id="issuerow12475632" rel="12475632" data-issuekey="CXF-3016" class="issuerow">
                                            <td class="project">    CXF
</td>
                                            <td class="issuekey">

    <a class="issue-link" data-issue-key="CXF-3016" href="https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/CXF-3016">CXF-3016</a>
</td>
                                            <td class="summary"><p>
                User guides alignment for Camel, Servicemix, ActiveMQ, and CXF 
    </p>
</td>
                                            <td class="issuetype"> Improvement</td>
                                            <td class="status">
                Closed
    </td>
                                            <td class="priority">   Minor
</td>
                                            <td class="resolution">    Invalid
</td>
                                            <td class="assignee">    <em>Unassigned</em>
</td>
                                            <td class="reporter">            Robert Liguori
    </td>
                                            <td class="creator">            Robert Liguori
    </td>
                                            <td class="created"> 01/Oct/10 16:11 </td>
                                            <td class="lastViewed"> &nbsp; </td>
                                            <td class="updated"> 11/Oct/10 14:48 </td>
                                            <td class="resolutiondate"> 07/Oct/10 16:13 </td>
                                            <td class="versions">    &nbsp;
</td>
                                            <td class="fixVersions">                        Invalid            </td>
                                            <td class="components">                        Documentation            </td>
                                            <td class="duedate">    &nbsp;
</td>
                                            <td class="votes">0</td>
                                            <td class="watches">0</td>
                                            <td class="thumbnail"></td>
                                            <td class="timeoriginalestimate">864000</td>
                                            <td class="timeestimate">864000</td>
                                            <td class="timespent"></td>
                                            <td class="workratio">            0%
    </td>
                                            <td class="subtasks">                </td>
                                            <td class="issuelinks">                </td>
                                            <td class="environment"></td>
                                            <td class="description">      Consider the following users guide URLs of Camel, Servicemix, ActiveMQ, and CXF <br/>
<br/>
http://servicemix.apache.org/users-guide.html<br/>
http://camel.apache.org/user-guide.html<br/>
http://cxf.apache.org/docs/index.html<br/>
http://activemq.apache.org/getting-started.html<br/>
<br/>
All of these products provide SOA related solutions.<br/>
<br/>
Each one of the user guides appear to have been developed independent of the other related product&#39;s guides.<br/>
<br/>
It would be nice if they had the same feel and content structure.  Note: Of course each would have sections related to info that is unique to them.<br/>
<br/>
I&#39;m basically suggesting that a similair table of contents exists for each user guide, with the subcontents created/refined in a quality-controlled manner.<br/>
<br/>
This would require someone comparing all four user guides, and bringing them into alignment.  The exercise will be valuable as it will expose missing sections of each user guide and will encourage the hyperlinking of informaiton where necessary.<br/>
<br/>
In the long run, the existing, valuable user guides would be refined to produce four top quality user guides; one for each product: Camel, Servicemix, ActiveMQ, and CXF <br/>
<br/>
Please take this request under strong consideration.<br/>
  <br/>
<br/>
<br/>
<br/>

  </td>
