                                            <td class="description">      <br/>
Create a Community section in the CXF main page side bar, to be in somewhat of an alignment of Camel, ActiveMQ and ServiceMix main pages:<br/>
<br/>
Community<br/>
-- Support <br/>
-- Contributing <br/>
-- Discussion Forums <br/>
-- Mailing Lists <br/>
-- Users <br/>
-- Team <br/>
<br/>
<br/>
Notes:<br/>
<br/>
Community<br/>
-- Support (Move here from Users)<br/>
-- Contributing (Move here form Developers\Getting-Involved).<br/>
-- Discussion Forums (Link to CXF Discussion Forums, I don&#39;t know where it is)... example: http://servicemix.apache.org/discussion-forums.html<br/>
-- Mailing Lists (Move here from Apache CXF section)<br/>
-- Users (Create this section, similiar to Community\users sections of ServiceMix and ActiveMQ websites)<br/>
-- Team (Move &#39;People&#39; here from Apache CXF section)<br/>

  </td>
