                                            <td class="issuelinks">                </td>
                                            <td class="environment">      Add the following switches to all commands: -version, -V and -Q.
  </td>
                                            <td class="description">      Recommendation to have the following added to all the commands:<br/>
<br/>
-version<br/>
-V <br/>
-Q<br/>
<br/>
Notes: -V currently only exists for the WSDL Validator. -Q would be the same usage as -quiet, it is uppercase to be consistent with -V that was used for -verbose.  <br/>
<br/>
Reference (though not applicable): http://www.gnu.org/prep/standards/standards.html#Command_002dLine-Interfaces<br/>
<br/>
Note: Switches are also known as command-line parameters, command-line switches, options, and flags.
  </td>
