                <tr id="issuerow12477089" rel="12477089" data-issuekey="CXF-3059" class="issuerow">
                                            <td class="project">    CXF
</td>
                                            <td class="issuekey">

    <a class="issue-link" data-issue-key="CXF-3059" href="https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/CXF-3059">CXF-3059</a>
</td>
                                            <td class="summary"><p>
                 idl2wsdl fails when constant is used to define boundary of sequence.
    </p>
</td>
                                            <td class="issuetype"> Bug</td>
                                            <td class="status">
                Closed
    </td>
                                            <td class="priority">   Major
</td>
                                            <td class="resolution">    Fixed
</td>
                                            <td class="assignee">            Freeman Fang
    </td>
                                            <td class="reporter">            Freeman Fang
    </td>
                                            <td class="creator">            Freeman Fang
    </td>
                                            <td class="created"> 12/Oct/10 02:15 </td>
                                            <td class="lastViewed"> &nbsp; </td>
                                            <td class="updated"> 06/Dec/10 22:48 </td>
                                            <td class="resolutiondate"> 12/Oct/10 03:04 </td>
                                            <td class="versions">    &nbsp;
</td>
                                            <td class="fixVersions">                        2.2.12,                     2.3.1            </td>
                                            <td class="components">    &nbsp;
</td>
                                            <td class="duedate">    &nbsp;
</td>
                                            <td class="votes">0</td>
                                            <td class="watches">0</td>
                                            <td class="thumbnail"></td>
                                            <td class="timeoriginalestimate"></td>
                                            <td class="timeestimate"></td>
                                            <td class="timespent"></td>
                                            <td class="workratio">&nbsp;
</td>
                                            <td class="subtasks">                </td>
                                            <td class="issuelinks">                </td>
                                            <td class="environment"></td>
                                            <td class="description">      Run idl2wsdl on the following<br/>
<br/>
module TRY<br/>
{<br/>
     const unsigned short  idlMaxUserName   = 20;<br/>
     typedef sequence&lt;unsigned short, idlMaxUserName&gt; idlUserName; <br/>
};<br/>
<br/>
... you&#39;ll see that if fails. If you change the boundary of the sequence to a literal, the problem goes away<br/>
<br/>
module TRY<br/>
{<br/>
        typedef sequence&lt;unsigned short, 20&gt; idlUserName; <br/>
};<br/>
<br/>
but according to the CORBA 2.4 spec, any constant expression that evaluates to yield a positive integer can be used to specify the upper bound of a sequence.<br/>
<br/>

  </td>
