                                            <td class="issuelinks">                </td>
                                            <td class="environment">      Windows, Java build 1.6.0_21-b07
  </td>
                                            <td class="description">      This bug affects endpoints, which have schema validation enabled and also contain a wsdlLocation. If a schema of the WSDL holds a reference to a DTD, the resolution of the DTD fails. These results in the fact that schema validation is repealed. This issue has already been raised on the mailing list (cf. http://cxf.547215.n5.nabble.com/SAXException-resolving-resource-http-www-w3-org-2001-XMLSchema-dtd-td551217.html and http://cxf.547215.n5.nabble.com/SAXException-resolving-resource-http-www-w3-org-2001-XMLSchema-dtd-td3200050.html , respectively).<br/>
<br/>
The resulting stacktrace is: <br/>
<br/>
12.10.2010 10:12:06 org.apache.cxf.wsdl.EndpointReferenceUtils createSchema<br/>
WARNUNG: SAXException for newSchema()<br/>
