                <tr id="issuerow12477252" rel="12477252" data-issuekey="CXF-3064" class="issuerow">
                                            <td class="project">    CXF
</td>
                                            <td class="issuekey">

    <a class="issue-link" data-issue-key="CXF-3064" href="https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/CXF-3064">CXF-3064</a>
</td>
                                            <td class="summary"><p>
                JAX-RS SSL on Google App Engine
    </p>
</td>
                                            <td class="issuetype"> Improvement</td>
                                            <td class="status">
                Closed
    </td>
                                            <td class="priority">   Major
</td>
                                            <td class="resolution">    Won&#39;t Fix
</td>
                                            <td class="assignee">    <em>Unassigned</em>
</td>
                                            <td class="reporter">            Gary Rudolph
    </td>
                                            <td class="creator">            Gary Rudolph
    </td>
                                            <td class="created"> 13/Oct/10 16:39 </td>
                                            <td class="lastViewed"> &nbsp; </td>
                                            <td class="updated"> 31/Mar/17 19:37 </td>
                                            <td class="resolutiondate"> 28/Mar/17 18:37 </td>
                                            <td class="versions">                        2.2.11            </td>
                                            <td class="fixVersions">                        Invalid            </td>
                                            <td class="components">                        JAX-RS,                     Transports            </td>
                                            <td class="duedate">    &nbsp;
</td>
                                            <td class="votes">2</td>
                                            <td class="watches">3</td>
                                            <td class="thumbnail"></td>
                                            <td class="timeoriginalestimate"></td>
                                            <td class="timeestimate"></td>
                                            <td class="timespent"></td>
                                            <td class="workratio">&nbsp;
</td>
                                            <td class="subtasks">                </td>
                                            <td class="issuelinks">                </td>
                                            <td class="environment"></td>
                                            <td class="description">      I&#39;ve been using JAX-RS with CXF with Google App Engine with success as a service provider as well as client proxies. Unfortunately, when a jaxrs spring injected client needs https I run into issues as the GAE {{HttpURLConnection}} is non-standard and doesn&#39;t contain the method {{getSSLSocketFactory}}.<br/>
<br/>
I noticed that {{TLSClientParameters}} now contains a {{setSSLSocketFactory}}, but it&#39;s not exposed through the spring xsd. Can we please change the {{&lt;http:tlsClientParameters&gt;}} xsd to support injecting the {{sslSocketFactory}}? Then I could get it from GAE and do it myself.<br/>
<br/>
The other option is to have {{HttpsURLConnectionFactory.decorateWithTLS}} attempt to get the {{SSLSocketFactory}} using {{SSLSocketFactory.getSSLSocketFactory}}.<br/>
<br/>
Note, I&#39;m doing the following in a spring config:<br/>
{code:xml}<br/>
&lt;http:conduit id=&quot;where-twilio-conduit&quot; name=&quot;https://api.twilio.com/*&quot;&gt;<br/>
	&lt;!--  FIXME: This will work if we can figure out a way to set sslSocketFactory to SSLSocketFactory.getSSLSocketFactory --&gt;<br/>
	&lt;http:tlsClientParameters useHttpsURLConnectionDefaultSslSocketFactory=&quot;true&quot; disableCNCheck=&quot;true&quot;/&gt;<br/>
	&lt;http:authorization&gt;<br/>
		&lt;sec:UserName&gt;foo&lt;/sec:UserName&gt;<br/>
		&lt;sec:Password&gt;bar&lt;/sec:Password&gt;<br/>
	&lt;/http:authorization&gt;<br/>
&lt;/http:conduit&gt;<br/>
&lt;jaxrs:client id=&quot;where-twilio-resource&quot; address=&quot;https://api.twilio.com/2008-08-01&quot; serviceClass=&quot;com.lolay.where.service.support.TwilioResource&quot;&gt;<br/>
	&lt;jaxrs:features&gt;<br/>
		&lt;cxf:logging/&gt;<br/>
	&lt;/jaxrs:features&gt;<br/>
&lt;/jaxrs:client&gt;<br/>
{code}<br/>
Then, I&#39;m receiving the following error:<br/>
{noformat}<br/>
Oct 13, 2010 4:05:56 PM org.apache.cxf.transport.https.SSLUtils getCiphersuites<br/>
INFO: The cipher suites have not been configured, falling back to cipher suite filters.<br/>
Oct 13, 2010 4:05:56 PM org.apache.cxf.transport.https.SSLUtils getCiphersuites<br/>
INFO: The cipher suite filters have not been configured, falling back to default filters.<br/>
