                                            <td class="resolutiondate"> 15/Oct/10 06:28 </td>
                                            <td class="versions">                        2.3            </td>
                                            <td class="fixVersions">                        2.3.1,                     2.4            </td>
                                            <td class="components">                        Transports            </td>
                                            <td class="duedate">    &nbsp;
</td>
                                            <td class="votes">0</td>
                                            <td class="watches">0</td>
                                            <td class="thumbnail"></td>
                                            <td class="timeoriginalestimate"></td>
                                            <td class="timeestimate"></td>
                                            <td class="timespent"></td>
                                            <td class="workratio">&nbsp;
</td>
                                            <td class="subtasks">                </td>
                                            <td class="issuelinks">                </td>
                                            <td class="environment"></td>
                                            <td class="description">      It seems the http client transport is not following redirects (HTTP 301 responses) to GET requests, even if the setAutoRedirect(true) is used. That seems to only work for POST requests.
  </td>
